   "tagline": "A Rutherford-scattering studio for the **155th birthday of Ernest Rutherford** (born **30 Aug 1871**, Brightwater, New Zealand) — the man who, forty years later in Manchester, read the 1-in-8000 backscattering his students Geiger and Marsden found in 1909 and concluded the atom is almost entirely empty, with all its positive charge in a **nucleus** ~20,000× smaller than the atom itself.",
